WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.650
The gift of life isn't the only thing the
survivors of Infinity War will get in the

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.820
fourth Avengers movie.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.060
According to leaked promo art for the sequel
that's emerged on the internet, they'll also

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.920
be getting some slick new suits.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.600
At least, it looks like Thor and Rocket will
and just in time for Halloween.

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:19.780
The artwork in question looks to be the back
side of packaging for an Avengers-related

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.960
toy, and while the leaked photo isn't high-quality,
it does give fans an idea of what a few Marvel

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.080
heroes might be wearing in Avengers 4.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.119
Accented with red patches, the suits are a
shiny, silver-white color along the torso,

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.300
arms, and sides of the legs, and black everywhere
else.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.600
Thor sports a thick, black Avengers "A" on
the chest-plate of his suit, and wields what

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.200
looks like an upgraded version of his newest
weapon, the hammer-ax hybrid Stormbreaker.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.180
And though Rocket appears unarmed, the ingenious
space rodent is probably still pretty dangerous.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:50.740
"What is that"

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.220
"A bomb"

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.379
"And you leave it laying around?"

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.940
"I was gonna put it in a box"

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.260
Taking a closer look at the photo, you'll
notice that Captain America also seems to

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.920
be wearing one of these new suits.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.900
To the left of the Star-Spangled Avenger is
the spacefaring Captain Marvel and she doesn't

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.280
have a white suit, apparently.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.180
Instead, she's seen wearing her standard red,
navy, and gold getup from the comic books,

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.790
which we previously got a glimpse of in the
trailer for the Captain Marvel movie.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.920
It makes sense that Carol Danvers would be
donning her signature suit rather than getting

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.299
the same outfit as the rest of the Avengers,
as she'll probably be introduced in Avengers

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.160
4 as a mysterious outsider, known only to
Nick Fury.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.640
It's sort of like in Grease, when Sandy wanted
to join the Pink Ladies.

00:01:30.649 --> 00:01:34.299
She couldn't just show up and score one of
those sweet bubblegum pink jackets she had

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.240
to earn it.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.380
Captain Marvel just might have to do the same thing.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.600
Thor, Rocket, and Cap's suits evoke the costume
Hank Pym wore when he was leaping through

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.260
the Quantum Realm in search of Janet Van Dyne.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:48.939
Which makes sense a popular Avengers 4 fan
theory suggests that the heroes who didn't

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:53.259
dissolve into dust in Infinity War might use
the Quantum Realm in their quest to rescue

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.590
all the people Thanos snapped away.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.980
So, what could all this mean?

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.000
The text in the photo appears to read, "The
Asgardian Thor wields the mighty Stormbreaker

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.820
in his battle against his foes.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:08.380
Rocket teams up with a new crew to guard the
galaxy against an even greater threat."

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.890
If this leak is legit, then that "new crew"
line all-but-guarantees it that Rocket is

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.200
joining the Avengers — for this movie, at
least.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:19.660
Thor and Captain America might be Rocket's
closest companions on the team, given that

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.760
all three are shown wearing the same silvery-white
costumes.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.100
One could theorize that the trio will partner
together on an adventure of their own.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.680
Specifically, they might be slipping into
the new suits to travel through the Quantum

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:36.190
Realm, locating time vortexes, skipping around
in the past, and stopping Thanos from committing

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:39.300
mass genocide before he even gets a chance
to start.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.240
It would make sense for these three to go
on their own literal mini-mission, much like

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.940
the characters did in Infinity War.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.800
That's kind of the only way to build a story
around a cast this big.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.170
Avengers 4 co-directors Joe and Anthony Russo
haven't confirmed much of anything about the

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.420
forthcoming superhero sequel not even its
title.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.820
So we can't be certain that these costumes
are real, or if the movie will truly feature

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.560
the team using time travel to take down Thanos.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.940
It isn't uncommon for toy companies to create
alternate costumes that characters never wear

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.990
in films a toy for Infinity War showed Hulk
busting out of the Hulkbuster suit, and that

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:14.080
never happened in the movie.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.200
So maybe these suits are only for Avengers
4 action figures and not Avengers 4 actors.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.180
And all the ideas about the film utilizing
the Quantum Realm?

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.540
Well, they're pretty compelling theories,
but until the filmmakers confirm them, they're

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.320
just theories.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.320
Sourceless leaks and unconfirmed speculation
aside, it's clear that the pieces of the Avengers

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.500
4 puzzle are slowly but surely starting to
come together, especially now that the movie

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.650
has wrapped filming.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:44.440
As Avengers 4 inches closer to its May 3rd,
2019 launch date and starts its official marketing

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.850
campaign, we should get a better idea of what's
legitimate and what's just another product

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.350
of the ever-moving rumor mill.

